From 11ab1900b8bd741954b8fbf543cc14d81160be42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yandong Lin <yandong.lin@rock-chips.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:24:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix[h265d]: Drop hdr meta pool

Depends on: b99c8e9704e8323cca476001b2fad6b91488dbb9
"fix[mpp_frame]: Refcount hdr dynamic meta for copy"

Since that commit, mpp_frame_set_hdr_dynamic_meta() copies the
meta into a refcounted wrapper owned by the frame, so frames no
longer depend on the parser side buffer lifetime. Replace the
hdr meta pool and its reference accounting with a plain reusable
current buffer:

- fill_dynamic_meta() just fills (and grows) the current buffer;
- h265d_frame_create() sets it on the frame, which copies it in;
- unref/recycle no longer touch meta, the stale meta pointer on
  the recycled frame is cleared at create.

This also removes the original pool leak where fill replaced
hdr_meta_current without putting the old slot, growing the pool
on every dynamic meta update. mpp_ref_pool has no other user and
is removed.

Signed-off-by: Yandong Lin <yandong.lin@rock-chips.com>
Change-Id: I82a56182e7a357b01d9a08688f09792d1817395f
